{
 "bank": "05",
 "sections": {
  "Layer3Ptr": {
   "name": "Layer 3 images, message box text and routine",
   "summary": [
    "$059000 Layer3Ptr: 45 three-byte pointers to Layer 3 (BG3) stripe images, 3 per tileset; index = 3 * [$1931] + [$1BE3] - 1 (see $00A02F). Most point at $059549.",
    "$059087-$05A57F: the stripe images, loaded with CODE_00871E. Record: VRAM address hi, lo; byte 3: bit 7 vertical, bit 6 RLE, low 6 bits = length hi; length lo",
    "  (bytes - 1); then tile/attribute pairs (RLE: one pair, repeated). A first byte with bit 7 set ends the image. Purpose of each image not verified.",
    "$05A580-$05B0FE: message box data: text row VRAM addresses, level-to-message table, message text offsets, and the text. Text codes: A-Z = $00-$19, a-z = $40-$59,",
    "  $1A ! , $1B . , $1D , , $1E ? , $1F space, $5D apostrophe; bit 7 = last character of the 18-tile row (rest of the row is blank).",
    "$05B0FF: stripe image $09 (blank fill that erases the text box). $05B106-$05B10B: three 2-entry tables for the box animation.",
    "$05B10C: message box routine, called by InLevelGameMode ($00A1DF) while [$1426] != 0. State [$1B88] = 0: window grows (+4 per frame in [$1B89], max $50),",
    "  at $4C the text is built; press a button to close ([$1B88] = 1: shrinks, text erased at $50). In the intro level or a Switch Palace it ends the level.",
    "Quirk: this section ends at $05B15D, in the middle of the routine; the rest (SubSideExit..) continues in the next section."
   ]
  }
 },
